speechtext:
Agreed.
Mr. Macdonald (Rosedale) I move:
That the Standing Committee on Health, Welfare and Social Affairs be empowered to study the subject matter of tobacco advertising;
That the orders for second reading of Bills C-34, C-69, and C-70 be discharged, and the subject matter thereof be referred to the committee;
And that the evidence adduced by the committee in its study of the subject matter of Bills C-39, C-45, C-53, C-134, C-137, and C-147 in the first session of the twenty-eighth Parliament be referred to the committee.
